  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Password Storage Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Password Storage Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Hash, Don't Encrypt",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Store a ==slow, salted hash==, never the password",
                "Hash = {green:one-way}; encryption = {red:reversible}",
                "Never store an encrypted copy either"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Salt vs Pepper",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Salt",
                "Pepper"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Value",
                  "Random, per user",
                  "One app-wide secret"
                ],
                [
                  "Kept",
                  "Beside hash, in clear",
                  "Env var or KMS"
                ],
                [
                  "Defeats",
                  "Rainbow tables, equal hashes",
                  "DB leak alone"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Password",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "+ salt",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Slow hash",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Store",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Why Fast Hashes Fail",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "MD5, SHA-1, plain SHA-256 are {red:fast}",
                "A GPU tries ==billions== per second",
                "Use a slow, tunable password hash"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "==Slow + salted== hash in the DB; the pepper lives outside it."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not encrypt?** Reversible: one key leak exposes every password.",
                "**Salt stops what?** Rainbow tables; not brute force on a weak password.",
                "**Salt vs pepper?** Salt: per user, stored. Pepper: secret, kept outside the DB.",
                "**SHA-256 alone?** Too fast: GPUs try billions per second."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "bcrypt and argon2 in Practice",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "bcrypt and argon2 in Practice",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. bcrypt",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cost n = ==2^n rounds==; +1 **doubles** the time",
                "Tune to ~==250 ms== per hash; cost 12 to start",
                "Salt is generated and **embedded** by bcrypt",
                "{red:72-byte limit}: input silently truncated; pre-hash or cap length"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. argon2id",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==argon2id== is the current default",
                "**Memory-hard**: resists GPU/ASIC attacks",
                "Tuned by memory, iterations, parallelism",
                "OWASP minimum: ==19 MiB==, t=2, p=1"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Usage",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Verify re-derives the hash from the stored salt"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const hash = await argon2.hash(pw);",
                "const ok = await argon2.verify(hash, pw);",
                "const h2 = await bcrypt.hash(pw, 12);",
                "const ok2 = await bcrypt.compare(pw, h2);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never ==",
              "text": "Compare hashes with verify/compare, not `==`: timing leak."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why argon2id?** Memory-hard, so GPUs/ASICs gain little",
                "**Cost factor?** 2^n rounds; +1 doubles time",
                "**Upgrade hashes?** Rehash on login when params are old",
                "**Salt location?** Inside the hash string"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sessions vs JWT",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Sessions vs JWT",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Session vs JWT",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Session",
                "JWT"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Client holds",
                  "opaque ID cookie",
                  "signed token"
                ],
                [
                  "Server state",
                  "yes (shared store, Redis)",
                  "none"
                ],
                [
                  "Revoke",
                  "==instant==: delete row",
                  "not before `exp` (denylist)"
                ],
                [
                  "Payload",
                  "stays on server",
                  "base64, readable"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "JWT = `header.payload.signature` with claims `sub`, `exp`",
                "Payload is ==encoded, not encrypted==: no secrets in it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Expiry and revocation",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Access token",
                    "note": "about 15 min",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Expires",
                    "note": "API returns 401",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Refresh token",
                    "note": "rotates on use",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New pair",
                    "note": "old refresh dead",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Verify every token",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Pin== allowed `algorithms`; reject `alg=none` and RS256-to-HS256 confusion",
                "Check signature, `exp`, `iss`, `aud`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "jwt.verify(token, publicKey, {",
                "  algorithms: [\"RS256\"],",
                "  issuer: \"auth.example.com\",",
                "  audience: \"api\",",
                "});"
              ],
              "note": "exp is checked by default"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**When sessions?** Instant revoke, one backend.",
                "**Revoke a JWT?** Short `exp`, rotate refresh, denylist.",
                "**localStorage risk?** XSS reads it; use an HttpOnly cookie.",
                "**Signature proves?** Untampered, signed by key holder."
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Logout is not revoke",
              "text": "Deleting the client token does not kill a JWT before ==exp==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Session Fixation and MFA",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Session Fixation and MFA",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Session Fixation",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Attacker plants ID",
                    "sub": "known session ID",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Victim logs in",
                    "sub": "uses that ID",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Server keeps ID",
                    "sub": "now authenticated",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Attacker shares session",
                    "sub": "same ID",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fix: ==regenerate the ID== on login and on any privilege change",
                "**Invalidate** the old ID",
                "Never accept IDs from ==URLs=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cookie Hardening",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Setting",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`HttpOnly`",
                  "No JS access"
                ],
                [
                  "`Secure`",
                  "HTTPS only"
                ],
                [
                  "`SameSite=Lax` / `Strict`",
                  "CSRF defence"
                ],
                [
                  "Idle + absolute timeout",
                  "Caps a stolen session's life"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. MFA Factors",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Something you **know**, something you **have**, something you **are**."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Rank",
                "Factor",
                "Catch"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "1 (weakest)",
                  "SMS OTP",
                  "{red:SIM-swap}"
                ],
                [
                  "2",
                  "TOTP app",
                  "30s codes, shared secret"
                ],
                [
                  "3",
                  "WebAuthn / passkeys",
                  "{green:Phishing-resistant}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Fixation fix?** Regenerate the session ID on login.",
                "**HttpOnly?** Stops JS reading the cookie (XSS theft), not XSS actions or CSRF.",
                "**Why is SMS weakest?** SIM-swap, and codes can be phished.",
                "**Recovery codes?** Single-use, stored hashed, shown once; regenerate after use."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Broken Access Control and IDOR",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Broken Access Control and IDOR",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Who vs What",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Authentication**: who you are",
                "**Authorization**: what you may do",
                "==Broken access control== (OWASP A01): missing or wrong server-side check",
                "Hidden buttons and UI checks are {red:not security}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. IDOR and the Fix",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "GET /invoices/101",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Change to 102",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "No owner check",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Other user's data",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Check ownership {green:server-side} on every request",
                "==Deny by default==",
                "Use the session identity, not a client ID"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SELECT * FROM invoices",
                "WHERE id = ?",
                "AND owner_id = session.user_id"
              ],
              "note": "no row = 404"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Escalation and Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Example",
                "Test"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Horizontal",
                  "user A reads user B",
                  "swap B's ID"
                ],
                [
                  "Vertical",
                  "user hits `/admin`",
                  "call admin route as user"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "UUIDs are not a fix",
              "text": "Random IDs only ==obscure== the object; the missing check remains."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**IDOR vs escalation?** IDOR swaps an object ID; escalation gains a higher role",
                "**Test IDOR?** Two accounts: replay A's request with B's ID",
                "**UUIDs enough?** No, only hides IDs",
                "**Checks live where?** Server, every request"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Auth Security Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Auth Security Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Passwords",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==argon2id== or bcrypt cost 12+",
                "**Unique salt** per user; optional pepper in KMS",
                "Constant-time compare, never `==`",
                "Rehash on login when parameters change"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sessions, JWT, Cookies",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Session",
                "JWT"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Holds",
                  "Opaque ID",
                  "Signed claims"
                ],
                [
                  "Revoke",
                  "Delete row",
                  "Short `exp` + refresh"
                ],
                [
                  "Verify",
                  "Store lookup",
                  "Pin alg, check `exp`"
                ],
                [
                  "Secrets",
                  "Server side",
                  "Never in payload"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cookie: ==HttpOnly==, ==Secure==, ==SameSite=Lax==",
                "New session ID on login and privilege change (stops fixation)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Access Control",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Deny by default==",
                "Check ownership server-side every request",
                "Use session identity, not client IDs",
                "MFA for sensitive actions, prefer ==WebAuthn=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "IDOR",
              "text": "`WHERE id = ? AND owner_id = session.user_id`. UUIDs only hide IDs."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Secure login?** Rate-limit, verify hash, new session ID, secure cookie, MFA",
                "**Top three mistakes?** Fast hashes, unpinned JWT or loose cookies, missing ownership checks",
                "**Audit IDOR?** Two accounts: replay A's IDs with B's session; expect 403"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A site keeps the same session ID after login. An attacker planted `sid=abc` in the victim's browser first. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The attacker's `sid=abc` becomes the logged-in session.",
                "Fix: ==regenerate the ID== on login and invalidate the old one."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Invoices use random UUIDs, but the query is `WHERE id = ?`. User A pastes B's invoice UUID. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "B's invoice is returned: UUIDs hide IDs, they do not authorize.",
                "Add `AND owner_id = session.user_id`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "bcrypt cost goes from 12 to 14. Roughly how does hash time change?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "About 4x longer: cost n means 2^n rounds.",
                "Old hashes still verify, so rehash on next login."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}